### Purchase Orders — requires auth + tenant header
### Set variables after login (default tenant id = 1 for sari-sari seed)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}
@tenantId = 1

### Login (adjust email/password to your demo user)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@example.com",
  "password": "password"
}

### Create purchase order
# @name createPo
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplierName": "ABC Distributors",
  "notes": "Weekly restock",
  "expectedDeliveryDate": "2026-05-30",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "NOOD-001", "quantity": 50 },
    { "sku": "CAN-001", "quantity": 20, "unitCost": 110.00 }
  ]
}

### List purchase orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}

### Get purchase order by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/purchase-orders/{{createPo.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}

### Receive goods (partial or full)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/purchase-orders/{{createPo.response.body.id}}/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "NOOD-001", "quantityReceived": 50 },
    { "sku": "CAN-001", "quantityReceived": 20 }
  ]
}
